**OPRO** (Optimization by PROmpting, Yang et al., Google DeepMind, 2023) makes the LLM itself the optimizer. Its **meta-prompt** has three parts:

- the **optimization trajectory**: previously tried instructions with their training accuracy, **sorted in ascending order** so the best sit at the end;
- a few **task exemplars** (3 random training examples per step) showing where the instruction is inserted;
- **meta-instructions**, such as "Write your new text that is different from the old ones and has a score as high as possible."

Where APE paraphrases one good candidate, OPRO lets the optimizer see the whole history of what scored well and badly.

